# Teams Notify Trigger

When the user includes `/teams-notify`, says "notify Teams", "post to Teams",
"Teams ping", or asks to "send this to Teams", treat it as an explicit request
to run the Teams notification script.

Required behavior:

- Read and follow `.cursor/skills/teams-notify/SKILL.md`.
- Do not only acknowledge the request in chat; run
  `.cursor/skills/teams-notify/scripts/Send-TeamsNotify.ps1` from the repo root.
- Send the same substantive answer the user should read in Cursor, not skill
  documentation, placeholder text, or a generic "done" unless the user clearly
  asked only for a connectivity test.
- If the user provides `Teams chat title: <title>`, pass that value as
  `-ChatName`.
- If the user asks for the Cursor tab title to appear in Teams but no title is
  provided and `TEAMS_NOTIFY_CHAT_NAME` is unavailable, ask once for the exact
  tab title before sending.
- Never print, log, commit, or include the webhook URL. The script must resolve
  it from `TEAMS_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL`.

`/teams-notify` is an agent instruction, not a native Cursor command. The agent
must invoke the PowerShell script for a Teams message to be sent.
